# oracle: the slater example's pair style, hybrid/overlay dpd 1.0 1.0 245455 + coul/slater/long 0.929 3.0 with ewald 1e-5, 200 atoms (+1/-1 and a neutral dpd species) in a 10^3 periodic box, NVE 20 steps
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max relative error at or below 1e-14; the case passes at rel=1e-14 abs=0 (the tightest tolerance that holds).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-14 abs=0
units        lj
boundary     p p p
atom_style   charge
region       simBox block 0 10 0 10 0 10
create_box   3 simBox
create_atoms 1 random 100 1234 simBox
create_atoms 2 random 50 5678 simBox
create_atoms 3 random 50 9012 simBox
set          type 2 charge -1.0
set          type 3 charge 1.0
comm_modify  mode single vel yes
mass         * 1.0
velocity     all create 1.0 4242
pair_style   hybrid/overlay dpd 1.0 1.0 245455 coul/slater/long 0.929 3.0
pair_coeff   * * dpd 25.0 4.5
pair_coeff   * * coul/slater/long
kspace_style ewald 1e-5
timestep     0.0005
fix          1 all nve
thermo_style custom step time temp pe ke ecoul elong evdwl
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo       5
run          20
